@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# dsv4-pd-mini: in-host P/D test plan (one v6e-8 host)
+
+Code: tpu-inference branch `pd-mini-dev` (worktree `dw-tpu-work/dsv4-pd-mini/wt`) = dsv4-prefill8 `mem2`
+(base 0001-0006 + prefill8 extras, all flag-gated) + this work:
+
+- `tpu_inference/distributed/tpu_connector_dsv4.py`: `TPUConnectorDSV4` (selected only via
+  `--kv-transfer-config kv_connector=TPUConnectorDSV4`). Fixes the stock `TPUConnectorHMA` for DSV4:
+  overlaid multi-group KV arrays + `_rope` companions, SWA/compressor-state groups transfer only the
+  tail window, full groups registered as 1024-token chunks so D pulls only chunks past its own prefix
+  hit and never overwrites cached blocks, P side-channel port carried in `kv_transfer_params`
+  (two P on one host). Logs `PDSEND` / `PDPULL` / `PDINSERT` JSON lines.
+- `tpu_platform.py`: allow-list `TPUConnectorDSV4`.
+- `sharding.py`: `attn_dp_size=1` with TP2 MLA divided by zero (`shard_divisor = 1 // 2`); clamped to 1.
+  Only that previously-crashing case changes.
+
+CPU evidence (titan-6, toy shapes): `tests/distributed/test_tpu_connector_dsv4_cpu.py` (7: real jax
+transfer server, DSV4-like overlaid arrays, exact row equality, hit/null blocks untouched, chunk skip,
+side-port notify + release) and `test_tpu_connector_dsv4_sched_cpu.py` (5: vLLM's real Scheduler as P
+and D with DSV4-shaped groups 1024-MLA x3 / SWA 64,w128 / state 4,w8 / state 8,w128, chunked prefill,
+D-side prefix hits 0/2048/4096: plan reads only existing P blocks, covers every block D needs, D
+recomputes exactly 1 token, P frees after notify). Router/workload/analysis tested against
+`fake_vllm.py`.
+
+Deployment: each copy is one `vllm serve` on a 2-chip subslice (TPU_VISIBLE_CHIPS pair,
+TPU_CHIPS_PER_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,2,1, TPU_PROCESS_BOUNDS=1,1,1), TP2 with
+`enable_dp_attention=true, attn_dp_size=1` (MLA requires DP attention; attn_dp=1 keeps a single vLLM
+scheduler; KV replicated on both chips), `--no-async-scheduling`, prefix caching on, fp8 KV,
+MNBT 2048, max_len 34816. P0 P1 = kv_producer on pairs 0,1; D0 D1 = kv_consumer on pairs 2,3. Router
+`pd_router.py` on :8000. Colocated reference C0 = same flags without connector on pair 0.
+
+## Steps (host time)
+
+0. deploy (5 min): `/opt/dsv4/pdmini/{tpu-inference,*.py,*.sh,prompts.json}`; PYTHONPATH puts this
+   tpu-inference ahead of the venv's editable install. Import check.
+1. mini checkpoint (10 min): `build_mini.py /opt/dsv4/ckpt/dsv4-flash-full /opt/dsv4/ckpt/dsv4-flash-5L`;
+   must print compress_ratios [0, 0, 4, 128, 4].
+2. chip pairs (5 min): `chip_probe.sh coords`, `chip_probe.sh pairs "0,1 2,3 4,5 6,7" 1,2,1` (fallback 2,1,1
+   or pairs by coords). Success = 4 concurrent PAIR_OK.
+3. raw transfer bandwidth (5 min): `xfer_micro.sh` (replicated vs sharded, 1 MB..1 GB).
+4. colocated reference (25 min): `pd_up.sh <run>/colo colo`; `correctness.py colo`; `xfer_sweep.py --mode colo`.
+5. P/D (30 min): `pd_up.sh <run>/pd pd`; `correctness.py pd`; `correctness.py compare`; `xfer_sweep.py --mode pd`.
+6. routing (40 min): warmup run; agent runs `--label aff1` (policy affinity) and `--label rr1` (policy rr via
+   POST /router/policy/rr), same sizes, different seeds; then a heavier pair (16 sessions x 8 turns).
+7. analysis: `analyze.py sweep`, `analyze.py routing`; report tpu-reports/2026-10-22/pd-mini-transfer-routing.md.
+
+## Success / failure
+
+- Correctness PASS = every case's 32 greedy tokens equal colocated (fresh, repeat, branch-4096 cases),
+  logprob diffs reported (bit-exact expected for P-computed positions; D recomputes the last prompt
+  token as a 1-token step, so the first token's logprob can differ by reduction order, as with a
+  colocated full prefix hit). Any token divergence = FAIL; investigate before measuring.
+- Transfer: PDPULL bytes/token constant across lengths (= KV layout bytes/token) + fixed tail; no
+  `timed_out`; D-side hits skip chunks (entries_pulled < entries_total on repeat/branch cases).
+- Routing: affinity puts >= 90% of follow-up turns on the copy holding the prefix (P and D), higher
+  P cached-token rate and D local-hit rate than rr, and fewer KV bytes pulled per request.
+
+## Fallbacks
+
+- `attn_dp_size=1` fails to load/run: try BOUNDS 2,1,1 / other pairs if it is a chip issue; if it is the
+  model path, P/D needs DP-scheduler support (per-rank block-id offsets for reqs_to_send/reqs_to_load in
+  dp_scheduler.py and replicated transfer shardings) -- see fallback patch notes in the report.
+- Transfer server bind issues: the host IP from `get_ip()` is used for all instances (single host).
